<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>
Performance comparison for selecting “maximum group size” <math id="Sx4.T4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. Utilizing Llama3.2 1B to analyze Perplexity across varying <math id="Sx4.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> values with <math id="Sx4.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>=256 for efficient experimentation. In the final row, the group size increases until the bit length reaches 4, indicating algorithm generalizability; here, the window is set to 4, and <math id="Sx4.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> represents the average group.
</figcaption>
