<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of <math id="A1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Firstly, we determine the lower bound of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Considering the case of group size 1 and number of group <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of non-zero elements <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. The cost is</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{g}0+\lambda\frac{1}{1}=n\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>g</mi></mover></mstyle><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{g}0+\lambda\frac{1}{1}=n\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The squared 2 norm is 0 since in the case of group size one <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}_{i}=\alpha_{i}\boldsymbol{B}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}_{i}=\alpha_{i}\boldsymbol{B}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider the case of the number of groups = <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-1</annotation></semantics></math>, so we have <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g-2</annotation></semantics></math> groups of size 1 and 1 group of size 2. The cost is</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{g-2}\left(0+\lambda\frac{1}{1}\right)+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{1}|-\alpha^{\ast})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{2}|-\alpha^{\ast})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{g-2}\left(0+\lambda\frac{1}{1}\right)+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{1}|-\alpha^{\ast})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{2}|-\alpha^{\ast})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum^{n-2}\left(0+\lambda\frac{1}{1}\right)+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{1}|-\frac{|a_{1}|+|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum^{n-2}\left(0+\lambda\frac{1}{1}\right)+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{1}|-\frac{|a_{1}|+|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{2}|-\frac{|a_{1}|+|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{n}(|a_{2}|-\frac{|a_{1}|+|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n-2)\lambda+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{2}|-|a_{1}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n-2)\lambda+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{2}|-|a_{1}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n-2)\lambda+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n-2)\lambda+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{1}{n}(\frac{|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|}{2})^{2}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n-2)\lambda+\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n-2)\lambda+\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Since we are minimizing the objective, when (<a href="#A1.Ex19" title="In Appendix A Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of 𝜆 ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A1.Ex25" title="In Appendix A Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of 𝜆 ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) we have n groups, else at most n-1 groups. Because we are using quantization for higher efficiency, a smaller group with a bigger size is desired, so we must avoid the n group case, such as we want (<a href="#A1.Ex19" title="In Appendix A Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of 𝜆 ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A1.Ex25" title="In Appendix A Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of 𝜆 ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;(n-2)\lambda+\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;(n-2)\lambda+\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}+\frac{\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}+\frac{\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{3\lambda}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{3\lambda}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{2n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\min_{1\leq i&lt;n}\frac{(|a_{i}|-|a_{i+1}|)^{2}}{3n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\min_{1\leq i&lt;n}\frac{(|a_{i}|-|a_{i+1}|)^{2}}{3n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since we want to avoid the n-1 group case too, and in general any group number leading to a small group size. So a good <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> will not be in the close neighbourhood of the actual lower bound, thus we can estimate the lower bound with a rough number</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}&gt;\min_{1\leq i&lt;n}\frac{(|a_{i}|-|a_{i+1}|)^{2}}{3n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}&gt;\min_{1\leq i&lt;n}\frac{(|a_{i}|-|a_{i+1}|)^{2}}{3n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We can just use the first two elements in the sorted array for fast computation and estimation of the lower bound of <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, so we have a lower bound</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda&gt;\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we deduce the upper bound for <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> with a similar method. Considering the case of one group, the cost is</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}|\boldsymbol{A}|Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}|\boldsymbol{A}|Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}nVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}nVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Considering two group of matrix <math id="A1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}_{1},\boldsymbol{A}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}_{1},\boldsymbol{A}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> split at <math id="A1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> sorted non-zero element of <math id="A1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, the cost is</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}|\boldsymbol{A}_{1}|Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+\frac{\lambda}{|\boldsymbol{A}_{1}|}+\frac{1}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}|\boldsymbol{A}_{2}|Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})+\frac{\lambda}{|\boldsymbol{A}_{2}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}|\boldsymbol{A}_{1}|Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+\frac{\lambda}{|\boldsymbol{A}_{1}|}+\frac{1}{|\boldsymbol{A}|}|\boldsymbol{A}_{2}|Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})+\frac{\lambda}{|\boldsymbol{A}_{2}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\left(kVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)+\frac{\lambda}{k}+\frac{\lambda}{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\left(kVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)+\frac{\lambda}{k}+\frac{\lambda}{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">If we want to have at least 2 group, (<a href="#A1.Ex38" title="In Appendix A Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of 𝜆 ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) <math id="A1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#A1.Ex36" title="In Appendix A Appendix B: Determining the Boundary of 𝜆 ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>),</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p17" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)+\frac{\lambda}{k}+\frac{\lambda}{n-k}&lt;\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{n}\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)+\frac{\lambda}{k}+\frac{\lambda}{n-k}&lt;\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\frac{\lambda}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})+\frac{n\lambda}{k}+\frac{n\lambda}{n-k}&lt;n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})+\frac{n\lambda}{k}+\frac{n\lambda}{n-k}&lt;n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})+\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{n\lambda}{k}+\frac{n\lambda}{n-k}-\lambda&lt;n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{n\lambda}{k}+\frac{n\lambda}{n-k}-\lambda&lt;n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda\left(\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1\right)&lt;n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda\left(\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1\right)&lt;n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda&lt;\frac{n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda&lt;\frac{n\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(k\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)\,\text{Var}(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Notice we can simplify the above expression by rewriting <math id="A1.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nVar(\boldsymbol{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nVar(\boldsymbol{A})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle nVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})=\sum_{x\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}}}(x-\mu)^{2}=\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}(x_{1}-\mu)^{2}+\sum_{x_{2}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}}}(x_{2}-\mu)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle nVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})=\sum_{x\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}}}(x-\mu)^{2}=\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}(x_{1}-\mu)^{2}+\sum_{x_{2}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}}}(x_{2}-\mu)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="A1.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is the average of elements of <math id="A1.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}(x_{1}-\mu)^{2}=\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}((x_{1}-\mu_{1})+(\mu_{1}-\mu))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}(x_{1}-\mu)^{2}=\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}((x_{1}-\mu_{1})+(\mu_{1}-\mu))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}(x_{1}-\mu_{1})^{2}+2(x_{1}-\mu_{1})(\mu_{1}-\mu)+(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}(x_{1}-\mu_{1})^{2}+2(x_{1}-\mu_{1})(\mu_{1}-\mu)+(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}\left((x_{1}-\mu_{1})^{2}+(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}\right)\right)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\sum_{x_{1}\in\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}}}\left((x_{1}-\mu_{1})^{2}+(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}\right)\right)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
