<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle kVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})+k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle kVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})+k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p26.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting this into the upper bound, we get</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p27" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{nVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(kVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{nVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}})-\left(kVar(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{1}})+(n-k)Var(\tilde{\boldsymbol{A}_{2}})\right)}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\max_{1\leq k&lt;n}\frac{k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\max_{1\leq k&lt;n}\frac{k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p28.1" class="ltx_p">We can further simplify the numerator.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p29" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k(\mu_{1}-\mu)^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\mu)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k(\mu_{1}-\frac{k\mu_{1}+(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\frac{k\mu_{1}+(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k(\mu_{1}-\frac{k\mu_{1}+(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\mu_{2}-\frac{k\mu_{1}+(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k(\frac{n\mu_{1}-k\mu_{1}-(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\frac{n\mu_{2}-k\mu_{1}-(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k(\frac{n\mu_{1}-k\mu_{1}-(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\frac{n\mu_{2}-k\mu_{1}-(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k(\frac{(n-k)\mu_{1}-(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\frac{-k\mu_{1}+k\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k(\frac{(n-k)\mu_{1}-(n-k)\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\frac{-k\mu_{1}+k\mu_{2}}{n})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k(\frac{(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\frac{-k(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})}{n})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k(\frac{(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})}{n})^{2}+(n-k)(\frac{-k(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})}{n})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k(n-k)^{2}(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}+(n-k)k^{2}(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{n^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k(n-k)^{2}(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}+(n-k)k^{2}(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{n^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{kn-k^{2}+k^{2}}{n^{2}}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{kn-k^{2}+k^{2}}{n^{2}}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{k}{n}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{k}{n}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p30.1" class="ltx_p">So the upper bound is</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p31" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda&lt;\max_{1\leq k&lt;n}\frac{\frac{k}{n}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda&lt;\max_{1\leq k&lt;n}\frac{\frac{k}{n}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p32.1" class="ltx_p">Keep in mind we want to balance the efficiency and accuracy, so we don’t want to get too close to the precise upper bound, which only considers efficiency; hence, we can estimate the upper bound with a faster calculation. Using <math id="A1.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=\frac{n}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\frac{n}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p33" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex72.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{\frac{\frac{n}{2}}{n}(n-\frac{n}{2})(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{\frac{n}{\frac{n}{2}}+\frac{n}{n-\frac{n}{2}}-1}&lt;\max_{1\leq k&lt;n}\frac{\frac{k}{n}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{\frac{\frac{n}{2}}{n}(n-\frac{n}{2})(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{\frac{n}{\frac{n}{2}}+\frac{n}{n-\frac{n}{2}}-1}&lt;\max_{1\leq k&lt;n}\frac{\frac{k}{n}(n-k)(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{\frac{n}{k}+\frac{n}{n-k}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{\frac{1}{2}(\frac{n}{2})(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{2+\frac{n}{\frac{n}{2}}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{\frac{1}{2}(\frac{n}{2})(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{2+\frac{n}{\frac{n}{2}}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\frac{n}{4}(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\frac{n}{4}(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{12}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p34.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we have</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p35" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{min}=\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}&lt;\lambda&lt;\frac{n(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{12}=\lambda_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{min}=\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}&lt;\lambda&lt;\frac{n(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{12}=\lambda_{max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p36" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p36.1" class="ltx_p">And we can control <math id="A1.p36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A1.p36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\lambda}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\lambda}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p37" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex77.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{min}+\tilde{\lambda}(\lambda_{max}-\lambda_{min})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{min}+\tilde{\lambda}(\lambda_{max}-\lambda_{min})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}+\tilde{\lambda}(\frac{n(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{12}-\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n}+\tilde{\lambda}(\frac{n(\mu_{1}-\mu_{2})^{2}}{12}-\frac{(|a_{1}|-|a_{2}|)^{2}}{3n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p38" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p38.1" class="ltx_p">A good <math id="A1.p38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> should be located somewhere in the latter half of the bound, not too close to the upper bound for quantization of LLMs. Notice that a precise <math id="A1.p38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> leads to a specific optimal group size that can be found via binary searching on the result group size from Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix A: Our Three Algorithms ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Since this is too computationally intensive, we guess <math id="A1.p38.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\lambda}=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\lambda}=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>. Empirical results shown <math id="A1.p38.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> have indifferent impact on quantization performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix C: Experiments and Evaluations</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents additional details regarding our experiments and evaluations. By providing granular details, we aim to ensure clarity and transparency, enabling readers to fully understand our experimental framework.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Seven QA tasks.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use seven QA tasks in our study: ARC-C (Abstraction and Reasoning Challenges) and ARC-E (Abstraction and Reasoning Corpus Easy) assess performance in complex/simple reasoning tasks; BooIQ measures accuracy in answering yes/no questions; HellaSwag tests ability in generating coherent text continuations; OPQA (Open-Book Question Answering) accesses performance in open book question answering; PIQA (Physical Interaction QA) evaluates commonsense reasoning in physical interactions; and Winogrande examines context-dependent ambiguity resolution. Avg. (Average Performance) is the average performance across these benchmarks provides a comprehensive overview of the models’ capabilities. The higher score in all these benchmarks suggests better model performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">PPL performance.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In LLMs, perplexity (PPL) measures the uncertainty of the model when predicting the next word. A lower perplexity indicates that the model is more confident in its predictions. We compare the PPL of our method against SOTA binary quantification and 4-bit quantification. From Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ PPL performance. ‣ Appendix B Appendix C: Experiments and Evaluations ‣ Binary Quantization For LLMs Through Dynamic Grouping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we can see that our method achieves performance comparable to FP in terms of perplexity, while outperforming the existing SOTA methods for both binary quantization and 4-bit quantization.</p>
</div>
